{"title":"Stablecoins competing with banks?","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/924243536/0/marginalrevolution~Stablecoins-competing-with-banks.html","date":1756838205000,"content":"<blockquote><p>Another concern is that stablecoins could displace bank deposits and undermine commercial banks. Many banks are taking steps to “tokenise” their deposits, allowing them to be used easily for blockchain-based transactions. And they are reducing their fat fees on cross-border payments. In other words, faced with new competition, they are cutting costs and increasing efficiency. This is as it should be.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.ft.com/content/72aa6431-366b-4409-b3ce-9a99d661473d\" target=\"_blank\">more from Eswar Prasad at the FT</a>.  Or can the banks simply not compete and will lose lots of deposits?</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/09/stablecoins-competing-with-banks.html\">Stablecoins competing with banks?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/924243536/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/924243536/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/924243536/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/924243536/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/924243536/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/email20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feed